Actually, if I unwrap `self.call` and then use it, it should work.

Wait, what if `self.call` is not a function but an object with `__call__`?
`inspect.unwrap` follows `__wrapped__` chain.

If `self.call` is a class, `inspect.unwrap(self.call)` will return the class.

